1
00:00:00,622 --> 00:00:08,459
(Q11（单选）) Presenter: My guest on the show today is Alice Riches who started the Street Play Scheme where she lives in Beechwood Road.

2
00:00:08,459 --> 00:00:15,954
For those of you that don't already know – Street Play involves local residents closing off their street for a few hours

3
00:00:15,954 --> 00:00:23,276
so that children have a chance to play in the street safely. She started it in her own street, Beechwood Road,

4
00:00:23,276 --> 00:00:28,125
and the idea caught on, and there are now Street Play Schemes all over the city.

5
00:00:28,125 --> 00:00:31,410
So when did you actually start the scheme, Alice?

6
00:00:31,410 --> 00:00:39,387
(Q11干扰项C) Alice:Well, I first had the idea when my oldest child was still a toddler, so that's about six years ago now

7
00:00:39,387 --> 00:00:44,017
(Q11干扰项A) but it took at least two years of campaigning before we were actually able to make it happen.

8
00:00:44,017 --> 00:00:47,282
[Q11答案句B： been up = take place, first] So the scheme's been up and running for three years now.

9
00:00:47,282 --> 00:00:54,857
(Q12) We'd love to be able to close our road for longer – for the whole weekend, from Saturday morning until Sunday evening,for example.

10
00:00:54,857 --> 00:01:02,032
[Q12答案句A + Q12干扰项C（时间干扰）] At the moment it's just once a week. But when we started it was only once a month. But we're working on it.

11
00:01:02,032 --> 00:01:05,350
(Q13) Presenter: So what actually happens when Beechwood Road is closed?

12
00:01:05,350 --> 00:01:13,863
[Q13答案句（C）， resident = local， warden原词] Alice:We have volunteer wardens, mostly parents but some elderly residents too, who block off our road at either end.&nbsp;

13
00:01:13,863 --> 00:01:21,940
[Q13干扰项A： council 偷换概念， 不符合 题干中的【事件】] The council have provided special signs but there's always a volunteer there to explain what's happening to any motorists.

14
00:01:21,940 --> 00:01:28,829
[Q13干扰项B： 提到police，但依然不符合题干中【动词 事儿 close the road】] Generally, they're fine about it – we've only had to get the police involved once or twice.

15
00:01:28,829 --> 00:01:33,716
(Q14) Now I should explain that the road isn't completely closed to cars.

16
00:01:33,716 --> 00:01:36,715
But only residents' cars are allowed.

17
00:01:36,715 --> 00:01:46,679
[Q14答案句（B）解释型同替= drive very slowly] If people really need to get in or out of Beechwood Road, it's not a problem – as long as they drive at under 20 kilometres per hour.

18
00:01:46,679 --> 00:01:53,187
[Q14干扰项A，不是 have to停到其他街道] But most people just decide not to use their cars during this time, or they park in another street.

19
00:01:53,187 --> 00:01:56,967
[Q14干扰项C： 也是偷换概念， 只是提到了warden而已] The wardens are only there to stop through traffic.

20
00:01:56,967 --> 00:02:00,683
(Q15) Presenter: So can anyone apply to get involved in Street Play?

21
00:02:00,683 --> 00:02:11,395
[Q15答案句（C） demand is the greatest = most] Alice:Absolutely – we want to include all kids in the city – especially those who live on busy roads.&nbsp;It's here that demand is greatest.

22
00:02:11,395 --> 00:02:24,567
[Q15干扰项A，B， 并列关系  （做题技巧）] Obviously, there isn't such demand in wealthier areas where the children have access to parks or large gardens,or in the suburbs where there are usually more places for children to play outside.

23
00:02:24,567 --> 00:02:30,288
(Q16) I'd recommend that anyone listening who likes the idea should just give it a go.

24
00:02:30,288 --> 00:02:37,423
We've been surprised by the positive reaction of residents all over the city. And that's not just parents.

25
00:02:37,423 --> 00:02:42,250
[Q16干扰项（A）] There are always a few who complain but they're a tiny minority.

26
00:02:42,250 --> 00:02:52,785
[Q16答案句（B） + 干扰项C，是有噪音的 不是lack of] On the whole everyone is very supportive and say they're very happy to see children out on the street – even if it does get quite noisy.

27
00:02:52,785 --> 00:02:58,029
(Q17&18（多选）) Alice:There have been so many benefits of Street Play for the kids.

28
00:02:58,029 --> 00:03:04,679
Parents really like the fact that the kids are getting fresh air instead of sitting staring at a computer screen,

29
00:03:04,679 --> 00:03:08,294
[Q19干扰项（A） 不符合 increased] even if they're not doing anything particularly energetic.

30
00:03:08,294 --> 00:03:14,818
[干扰项（E） ， 只是和朋友玩，不是new friends。 而且！ 不符合题干的 most important 程度限定词] And of course it's great that kids can play with their friends outside without being supervised by their parents –

31
00:03:14,818 --> 00:03:23,173
[Q17答案句（B） develop confidence without parents = indepence 解释型] but for me the biggest advantage is that kids develop confidence in themselves to be outside without their parents.

32
00:03:23,173 --> 00:03:31,932
[Q18答案句（D）： extended family = community 近义词] The other really fantastic thing is that children get to know the adults in the street – it's like having a big extended family.

33
00:03:31,932 --> 00:03:39,640
(Q19&20（多选）) Presenter: It certainly does have a lot of benefits. I want to move on now and ask you about a related project in King Street.

34
00:03:39,640 --> 00:03:48,651
Alice:Right. Well this was an experiment I was involved in where local residents decided to try and reduce the traffic along King Street,&nbsp;

35
00:03:48,651 --> 00:03:55,676
which is the busiest main road in our area, by persuading people not to use their cars for one day.

36
00:03:55,676 --> 00:04:02,621
We thought about making people pay more for parking – but we decided that would be really unpopular –

37
00:04:02,621 --> 00:04:08,681
so instead we just stopped people from parking on King Street but left the other car parks open.

38
00:04:08,681 --> 00:04:12,811
[🟢] It was surprising how much of a difference all this made.

39
00:04:12,811 --> 00:04:24,015
[Q19答案句（E） ： expected后不是答案【Q19干扰项C】， 听「unexpected」是什么] As we'd predicted, air quality was significantly better but what I hadn't expected was how much quieter it would be， even with the buses still running.

40
00:04:24,015 --> 00:04:35,537
[Q20答案句（A） amazed= 题干中surprise， sales in the shop went up =  more shoppers] Of course everyone said they felt safer but we were actually amazed that sales in the shops went up considerably that day,we thought there'd be fewer people out shopping – not more.（作为上一句的补充说明）

41
00:04:35,537 --> 00:04:38,037
Presenter: That's really interesting so the fact that …

